      "question": "Saturated steam at 100°C is condensing in the shell side of a shell and tube heat exchanger. Cooling water enters the tubes at 30°C and leaves at 70°C. Calculate the LMTD for counter flow arrangement:",
      "options": [
        "47.0°C",
        "47.2°C",
        "46.8°C",
        "None of the above"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Counter flow LMTD with steam at 100°C: ΔT1 = 100−30 = 70°C and ΔT2 = 100−70 = 30°C, so LMTD = (70−30)/ln(70/30) = 40/0.8473 ≈ 47.2°C. This matches the printed PDF stem and options.",
